("BDW","PEW","near","Crofton Pumping Station",R,51.35889,-1.62587,50,"Your train passes Crofton Pumping Station, on the train's {side}. Its Boulton & Watt steam engine of 1812 is the oldest working beam engine in the world still in its original engine house.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crofton_Pumping_Station",X),
("PEW","WSB","near","Edington Priory",L,51.27891,-2.10688,550,"Your train passes near Edington Priory church, on the train's {side}, built by William Edington, Bishop of Winchester, and consecrated in 1361.","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edington_Priory",X),
